003Cp class=\"translation-author\">  \u003C/p>\u003Cp>To beloved Tittabo.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>Italian translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7122-2511\">Valentina Mignosa\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>A Tittabo amata.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>According to Dubois the female name Τιτταβώ must be indigenous and should have the same radical as Τιτταλος, variant of Τιττελος attested in Thessaly. As for the disinence -ώ, and not -ώι as everywhere in the Doric context in Sicily, it's possible to explain it as a Ionism or an indigenous feature.\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Lentini 1982 181, fig. 8 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001878\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001878\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1984 34.0965 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Gallavotti 1985 35-36 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001971\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001971\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> 1985 35.1015 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000796\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Guarducci 1987 368, fig. 116 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001923\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001923\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Dubois 1989 \u003Ca href=\"http://www.persee.fr/doc/efr_0000-0000_1989_cat_119_1\" target=\"_blank\">1\u003C/a>  \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10000187\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Arena 1994 75, pl. XXI.1 \u003Ca href=\"ht